# SitecoreSilver site playbook

Human-readable copy: **`docs/SITECORESILVER.md`**. Agent copy: **`industry-verticals/sitecoresilver/AGENTS.md`**.

---

## Golden rules

1. **One component per task** — never the whole homepage in one prompt.
2. **Partial designs for site chrome** — header/footer in `Presentation/Partial Designs/`; page design composes them; pages use **`headless-main`** for content.
3. **`validate --fix`** before **`push -n production`** (from `authoring/`).
4. **SitecoreSilver paths only** — not other vertical starters in this repo.
5. Module auto-discovered via root `sitecore.json` → `authoring/items/**/*.module.json`.
6. **Editing host** in Deploy portal (name = `sitecoresilver`) **before** expecting Site Grouping to work.

---

## Presentation architecture (learn this pattern)

```text
Layout.tsx
  headless-header  ← Partial Design "header" (SitecoreSilverHeader + ds Default Header)
  headless-main    ← Page __Renderings (hero, grids, promos — page-specific only)
  headless-footer  ← Partial Design "footer" (SitecoreSilverFooter + ds Default Footer)

Page Design "DefaultPage"
  PartialDesigns = {header GUID}|{footer GUID}

Placeholder Settings/Partial Design/
  sxa-header, sxa-footer  (page-design slots — not the same as headless-* in Layout.tsx)
```

**YAML reference (serialized):**

| Item | Path |
|------|------|
| Partial design header | `sitecoresilver-site-root/sitecoresilver/Presentation/Partial Designs/header.yml` |
| Partial design footer | `.../Partial Designs/footer.yml` |
| Page design | `.../Page Designs/DefaultPage.yml` |
| Mapping | `.../Page Designs.yml` (TemplatesMapping → DefaultPage) |
| Header ds | `Data/Headers/Default Header.yml` |
| Footer ds | `Data/Footers/Default Footer.yml` |

**Do:** Put `SitecoreSilverHeader` / `SitecoreSilverFooter` in partial designs once.  
**Don't:** Repeat header/footer Json renderings on every page item.

Site-wide **Navigation** + **LinkList** children: prefer **inside partial designs** (under `/headless-header/sitecoresilver-header-nav-{*}` etc.). Home still has some children on the page — migrate when convenient.

Details: **`docs/SITECORESILVER.md#presentation-architecture-partial-designs--page-designs`**.

